# Build context exclusions for the four service images (apps/{api,worker,web,mcp}).
#
# This lives at the REPO ROOT on purpose. Every Dockerfile is built with the
# repo root as the context and `-f apps/<svc>/Dockerfile`, and buildx requires a
# .dockerignore in the CONTEXT — a per-app one would be ignored entirely.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE LISTED HERE
#   package.json, pnpm-lock.yaml, pnpm-workspace.yaml, .npmrc, tsconfig.base.json
#     The workspace install resolves @mcpedia/* through these. Excluding any of
#     them makes `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` either fail outright or
#     silently produce a different dependency graph than the one CI's gate
#     verified against pnpm-lock.yaml.
#   apps/*/package.json, packages/*/package.json
#     Same reason: pnpm links workspace packages from these manifests.
#   packages/db/drizzle/
#     The migrator reads the .sql journal off disk at runtime via
#     `new URL("../drizzle", import.meta.url)`. esbuild inlines only JS, so
#     dropping the journal makes the migrator find an empty folder and report
#     SUCCESS while changing nothing — the one build failure here that is silent.
#   apps/web/serve.mjs
#     Not a build output. It IS the web server, and it is stdlib-only on purpose.

# --- VCS / CI -----------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitignore

# --- Local state, never part of a build ---------------------------------------
.hermes
.moon/cache
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Build outputs: rebuilt inside the image, and copying the host's would
#     smuggle in stale or architecture-specific artifacts ------------------
**/dist
.moon

# --- Secrets and local env -----------------------------------------------------
# The services take their configuration from the environment at RUNTIME, injected
# by bws-exec (see the ExecStart lines in infra/systemd/*.service). Baking a .env
# into a layer would leak DATABASE_URL and BETTER_AUTH_SECRET into the image
# history forever, since a later layer cannot un-write an earlier one.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# --- Editor / OS noise ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea
.vscode

# --- Nix: the stack was DELETED, not merely unused ----------------------------
# flake.nix / flake.lock / web.nix are gone from the repo. The build-and-deploy
# path is now bundle-in-CI + scp (scripts/deploy-direct.sh), and Nix is not
# installed on the deploy host, so nothing here can run through it. The two
# `result` entries stay: they cost nothing and a stray `nix build` symlink
# accidentally copied into a context is exactly the kind of thing that should be
# excluded by name rather than by luck.
result
result-*

# --- Docs and agent metadata ----------------------------------------------------
*.md
!apps/*/README.md
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
